  <heading level="2">Simplify Expressions with Exponents</heading>
  <paragraph>Remember that an exponent indicates repeated multiplication of the same quantity. For example, $$2^{4}$$ means to multiply 2 by itself 4 times, so $$2^{4}$$ means $$2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2$$ .</paragraph>
  <paragraph>Let’s review the vocabulary for expressions with exponents.</paragraph>
  <note type="rule" source_type="Exponential Notation" title="Exponential Notation">
    <paragraph>This is read $$a$$ to the $$m^{th}$$ power.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the expression $$a^{m}$$ , the exponent $$m$$ tells us how many times we use the base $$a$$ as a factor.</paragraph>
  </note>
  <paragraph>Before we begin working with variable expressions containing exponents, let’s simplify a few expressions involving only numbers.</paragraph>
  <example number="6.16">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Simplify: ⓐ $$4^{3}$$ ⓑ $$7^{1}$$ ⓒ $$\left( \frac{5}{6} \right)^{2}$$ ⓓ $$(0.63)^{2}.$$</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>ⓐ</cell>
            <cell>$$4^{3}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply three factors of 4.</cell>
            <cell>$$4 \cdot 4 \cdot 4$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Simplify.</cell>
            <cell>$$64$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>ⓑ</cell>
            <cell>$$7^{1}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply one factor of 7.</cell>
            <cell>$$7$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>ⓒ</cell>
            <cell>$$\left( \frac{5}{6} \right)^{2}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply two factors.</cell>
            <cell>$$\left( \frac{5}{6} \right)\left( \frac{5}{6} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Simplify.</cell>
            <cell>$$\frac{25}{36}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>ⓓ</cell>
            <cell>$$(0.63)^{2}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply two factors.</cell>
            <cell>$$(0.63)(0.63)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Simplify.</cell>
            <cell>$$0.3969$$</cell>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
  <note type="practice" source_type="Try It" title="Try It" number="6.31">
    <paragraph>Simplify: ⓐ $$6^{3}$$ ⓑ $$15^{1}$$ ⓒ $$\left( \frac{3}{7} \right)^{2}$$ ⓓ $$(0.43)^{2}.$$</paragraph>
  </note>
