  </note>
  <heading level="2">Multiply Monomials</heading>
  <paragraph>Since a monomial is an algebraic expression, we can use the properties of exponents to multiply monomials.</paragraph>
  <example number="6.26">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Multiply: $$\left( {3x^{2}} \right)\left( {-4x^{3}} \right).$$</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$\left( {3x^{2}} \right)\left( {-4x^{3}} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Use the Commutative Property to rearrange the terms.</cell>
            <cell>$$3 \cdot (-4) \cdot x^{2} \cdot x^{3}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply.</cell>
            <cell>$$-12x^{5}$$</cell>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
  <note type="practice" source_type="Try It" title="Try It" number="6.51">
    <paragraph>Multiply: $$\left( {5y^{7}} \right)\left( {-7y^{4}} \right).$$</paragraph>
  </note>
  <note type="practice" source_type="Try It" title="Try It" number="6.52">
    <paragraph>Multiply: $$\left( {-6b^{4}} \right)\left( {-9b^{5}} \right).$$</paragraph>
  </note>
  <example number="6.27">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Multiply: $$\left( {\frac{5}{6}x^{3}y} \right)\left( {12xy^{2}} \right).$$</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$\left( {\frac{5}{6}x^{3}y} \right)\left( {12xy^{2}} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Use the Commutative Property to rearrange the terms.</cell>
            <cell>$$\frac{5}{6} \cdot 12 \cdot x^{3} \cdot x \cdot y \cdot y^{2}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply.</cell>
            <cell>$$10x^{4}y^{3}$$</cell>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
  <note type="practice" source_type="Try It" title="Try It" number="6.53">
    <paragraph>Multiply: $$\left( {\frac{2}{5}a^{4}b^{3}} \right)\left( {15ab^{3}} \right).$$</paragraph>
